What is Screen Scraping?

Screen Scraping is an RPA technique used to extract text and information from applications, websites, and computer screens.
-----------------------
UiPath provides 3 Screen Scraping Methods:

Full Text
Native
OCR (Optical Character Recognition)
----------------------------------------------

A. Full Text Method
Definition

Extracts text directly from the application's underlying text layer.

Working Principle
Reads actual text behind the UI.
Uses accessibility information.
No image processing required.
Works when text is selectable/readable by the system.
Advantages

✅ Very Fast

✅ High Accuracy

✅ Resource Efficient

Disadvantages

❌ Does not preserve text position/layout

❌ Fails if text is available only as an image

Example

Student Management System:

Student Name: Ravi
USN: 12345
Department: CSE

Full Text directly extracts:

Ravi
12345
CSE

Applications
Desktop applications
Web pages
Forms
Exam Point

Fastest method but does not preserve layout.
----------------------------------------------

B. Native Method
Definition

Extracts text using the application's native UI technology and preserves positional information.

Working Principle
Detects text elements.
Retrieves text and coordinates.
Maintains relative arrangement of text.
Advantages

✅ High Accuracy

✅ Preserves Layout

✅ Captures position of text

Disadvantages

❌ Slightly slower than Full Text

❌ Depends on application's UI technology

Example

Invoice Screen:

Invoice No: INV101
Date: 18/11/2026
Amount: ₹5000


Native Scraping extracts:

Invoice No → Position A
Date → Position B
Amount → Position C


and preserves their locations.

Applications
Structured desktop applications
Tables
Forms
Reports
Exam Point

Maintains layout and text position better than Full Text.
---------------------------------------------------------

C. OCR (Optical Character Recognition)
Definition

Extracts text from images, scanned documents, virtual machines, Citrix environments, and remote desktops.

Working Principle
Takes screenshot/image.
OCR engine recognizes characters.
Converts image text into editable text.
Advantages

✅ Works on images

✅ Works in Citrix and Remote Desktop

✅ Can read scanned PDFs

Disadvantages

❌ Slowest method

❌ Accuracy depends on image quality

❌ More processing required

Example

Image contains:

WELCOME TO BANK
Account Number: 123456


OCR converts image text to:

WELCOME TO BANK
123456

Applications
Scanned PDFs
Images
Citrix
Remote Machines
